    <DataNode elementId="AT3G10230-MONOMER" textLabel="AT3G10230-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q38933" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Encodes a protein with lycopene &amp;beta;-cyclase activity. This enzyme uses the linear, symmetrical lycopene as substrate. The enzyme introduces a ring at both ends of lycopene to form the bicyclic |FRAME:CPD1F-129| (&lt;i&gt;via&lt;/i&gt; the formation of the intermediate |FRAME:CPD1F-126|). The |FRAME:AT3G10230| gene from &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; was recombinantly expressed in engineered &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; strains modified to produced neurosporene or lycopene. In the former, the gene product led to the formation of |FRAME:CPD-7419|, whilst in the latter case, it led to the formation of &amp;beta;-carotene with no detectable &amp;gamma;-intermediate |CITS:[8837512]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G10230-MONOMER" />
